  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social, Economic and Environmental Drivers of Zoonoses in Tanzania (SEEDZ)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will examine and assess drivers, risks and impacts of zoonotic diseases - brucellosis, Q fever and Rift Valley Fever - that affect cattle, sheep and goats, and impact on human health, livelihoods and poverty in pastoral and peri-urban communities in Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
